Z||000003||DaRkLoRD||03-15-2000||12:59 AM||||I know it's none of my business what's happened with other people and their orders, but I fully intend to do business with Tom in the future. He's helped me a great deal with a recent project I've been working on, and I'm very grateful for his help. In my dealings with Tom, I have been quite satisfied. His work was perfect, and I wouldn't hesitate to ask him to do work for me again. Tom is a valuable asset to the Fiero community, as well as a friend to a lot of people here.<P>I'd really hate to see him leave, just because of a few problems with parts orders. I loaned a friend over $200, and he's had almost 3 years to pay it back. I've asked several times, and he keeps saying he can't afford it. I know many times he could afford it, but I'd rather have a friend than $200. I'm not sure how this relates to this particular situation, but I just felt like saying it. I don't care what some people might think, I trust Tom and look forward to ordering parts from him when I get my GT.<P>sorry for the long post.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Greg Piet||03-15-2000||02:49 AM||||Tom,<BR>I remembering ordering stuff from you and just shooting the Fiero breeze with you when I was a truly wet behind the ears with my Fiero.  I specifically ordered a stock subwoofer kit from you. You sent the product THE DAY I EMAILED YOU SAYING I SENT PAYMENT.   I thought that was extremely righteous of you, especially since the timing resulted in me getting the woofer before the weekend when i promptly installed the cool and good condition stuff i got from you.  I also could have been lying about sending the money for all you knew, but you trusted a fellow Fierophile and for both of us w/o a problem. <BR> I also remember the first thing I got for my fiero was from you.  It was a  radio faceplate.  you were extremly cool about it, and gave me an excellent description of what I would be getting...   To top it off the price was really fair!  <P>I actually felt bad when I got a short shifter from someone besides you, even though I realized you sold them after I got one.  I am a firm believer in repeat business at establishements that treat me right.  <P>Tom if you do leave Pennocks, can some of us still bug you if we are looking for a part?  I still have the original photocopy you sent with my faceplate in my folder of Fiero parts sources, and documentation so I have your number and address. ||||reg||1
