Z||000006||BOILERMAKER||03-15-2000||07:55 AM||||Man this really blows!!!  I guess everyone has spring fever or something.<P>Anyway, my experience with TOM has left me with nothing but a warm and fuzzy feeling.  I only bought a short shifter from him, but I believe in his email he said something like <BR>"I will send you the shifter and you can go ahead and send the check.  Fiero owners are usually very honest, so I am not worried about the money."  OK, maybe not word-for-word, but the thought is pretty much the same.<P>TOM, I hate that you are going through such a dilemna, and if there is absolutely ANYTHING I can do to help, then all you have to do is ask.||||reg||1
Z||000007||87ECO5||03-15-2000||12:58 PM||||I've had one experience with Tom and I was quite happy with it!<P>I inquired about a cigarette lighter in the mall section of the forum.  Tom responded quickly that he'd send one out to me - no charge!<P>I've heard lots of positive feedback about Tom.  Though I've not dealt with him much, I'd have to say he'll be dearly missed.<P><B>Tom, I wish the very best to you and your family!!!</B><p>[This message has been edited by 87ECO5 (edited 03-15-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||Oreif||03-15-2000||01:02 PM||||I can't believe this! I have not bought anything from Tom, But he has given his advice on repairing and working on my Fiero.<BR>His knowledge and experience is going to be greatly missed! I have had problems with vendor's in the past and I can relate to motorhead and v6, But flaming someone on an open forum is not the way to correct the differences. Especially when Tom has told everyone that he had other personal difficulties. I'm sure we have all had things in our life (other than Fiero problems) that has thrown a curve ball to us. It seems to me that it is always better to work things out as adults and use a little compassion in resolving issues. It does not seem that Tom was trying to rip-off anyone he just had some problems and it delayed other facets of his life. So now all his knowledge is gone.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Isn't it amazing how you never realize what you have lost until it's gone? I do hope that Tom can get through these difficult times and wish the best for him and his family. As usual this is just my $.02 worth.<BR>||||reg||1
